}], "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"dea8b5cd-f817-4d28-9ffb-60dcbc2b2889"],

Cell["\<\
Definition: a line is an inextensible geodesic \[LongDash] a shortest path \
that no neighbour of either end prolongs.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"e4699eb6-201a-4d74-b1a9-fb7ffa5e4bf6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Its graph \[LongDash] ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     Cell[
      TextData["InfraMeasurement"]], 
     "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraMeasurement", 
     "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
    "PackageLink",
    BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"], "[", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["g", "TI"], ",", " ", 
    StyleBox["line", "TI"], ",", " ", "\"\<Graph\>\""}], "]"}]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "39a534fd-6363-4ee7-805b-5bf342abd50d"],
 " \[LongDash] is a ",
 Cell[BoxData["List"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d9a53ac9-9047-400b-b78b-928b6b5cd8e7"],
 " of DAGs, one per pair of ends (",
 StyleBox["a", "TI"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["b", "TI"],
 ") that is compatible, ",
 StyleBox["d(a, b) = d(a, p) + d(p, q) + d(q, b)", "TI"],
 ", and maximal, no neighbour of ",
 StyleBox["a", "TI"],
 " or ",
 StyleBox["b", "TI"],
 " lengthening ",
 StyleBox["d(a, b)", "TI"],
 ". The DAG for (",
 StyleBox["a", "TI"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["b", "TI"],
 ") is the union of the intervals ",
 StyleBox["I(a, p)", "TI"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["I(p, q)", "TI"],
 " and ",
 StyleBox["I(q, b)", "TI"],
 ". Its chains are exactly the lines with those ends, and every line is a \
chain of exactly one DAG, so ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<Faithful\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "56938744-c5fb-494c-88d5-f7049e5b1292"],
 " is ",
 Cell[BoxData["True"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "cf7bee22-f4c4-4f8b-94b4-c7df602e6203"],
 "."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"91acc47e-6f73-47c8-bb04-376fe1d3dda2"],

Cell["\<\
The list is not optional. The union of the DAGs can carry chains that are not \
geodesics: through the edge 1\[Dash]2 of the 6-cycle there are three DAGs and \
three lines, while their union would add a fourth path that is not a geodesic.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"d527dbd1-f2fd-4366-a684-d7b721579387"],

Cell["\<\
The DAGs are alternatives, so the counts add across them. The family can be \
astronomical while the list stays small.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"9bbacb36-3010-4d61-95a3-ce79a2394ecb"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "With ",
 StyleBox["p", "TI"],
 " = ",
 StyleBox["q", "TI"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     Cell[
      TextData["InfraLine"]], 
     "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraLine", 
     "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
    "PackageLink",
    BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"], "[", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["p", "TI"], ",", " ", 
    StyleBox["p", "TI"]}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2dc4cc2a-2efb-43ef-8e7b-3d3127225c43"],
 " is every maximal geodesic through ",
 StyleBox["p", "TI"],
 ", once per orientation."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"70bd4fed-881e-4130-920e-5067a4354073"]
}, Open  ]],

